<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jón Sigurðsson</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1811–1879</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jón Sigurðsson was an Icelandic scholar and politician who led the nineteenth-century movement for Iceland's self-government from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/copenhagen">Copenhagen</a>. As president of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/althing">Althing</a> he pressed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a> for home rule, and the constitution of 1874 granted Iceland control over its own affairs. The Republic of Iceland was proclaimed on his birthday, 17 June, in 1944, now the national day.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jon-sigurdsson.jpg" alt="Jón Sigurðsson" width="320" height="440" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Þórarinn B. Þorláksson · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sigur%C3%B0sson_by_%C3%9Eorl%C3%A1ksson.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
